   184                          ;; PUSHRETADDR and caml_APPLY n, APPLY1, APPLY2, APPLY3:
   185                          ;;
   186                          ;; A closure application to n arguments is usually compiled by ocamlc by
   187                          ;; emitting a PUSHRETADDR (which pushes the return address onto the stack),
   188                          ;; followed by instructions that compute and push the arguments, and finally an
   189                          ;; APPLY n instruction that jump to the closure code; but when n < 4, ocamlc
   190                          ;; skips the PUSHRETADDR: its work is left up to APPLY1 (or APPLY2, or APPLY3).
   191                          
