   340                          ;; RESTART and GRAB:
   341                          ;;
   342                          ;; GRAB checks that the caller passed enough arguments onto the stack. If not,
   343                          ;; it creates a closure, stores all the available arguments in it, points the
   344                          ;; closure code to the instruction just before GRAB (which is assumed to be a
   345                          ;; RESTART), then returns to the caller, as if executing a RETURN instruction.
